&lt;!doctype html&gt;&lt;html&gt;&lt;head&gt;
  &lt;meta charset, viewport&gt;
  &lt;title&gt;, optional &lt;link&gt; to Google Fonts (Inter or Space Grotesk + a monospace like JetBrains Mono for numeric readouts)
  &lt;script type="importmap"&gt; — three@0.170.0 core + examples/jsm addons (OrbitControls, EffectComposer, RenderPass, UnrealBloomPass, CSS2DRenderer, BufferGeometryUtils) + simplex-noise@4.0.3, all pinned, all from cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/
  &lt;style&gt; — one block, organized as: :root design tokens (colors incl. 3 mode-accent vars, spacing, radii, shadows/glass blur), base reset, layout grid (topbar + canvas stage + side panel + bottom explain rail), glass-panel component class, buttons/sliders/toggle/select components, glossary popover component, drawer component, mode-switcher pills, neuron-mode canvas overlay grid, honesty-badge chips, responsive breakpoint (panel collapses to a bottom sheet under ~900px — nice-to-have per brief).
&lt;/head&gt;&lt;body&gt;
  &lt;header id="topbar"&gt; app name, 3-way mode switcher, quality toggle, "How this works" button, keyboard-hint icon
  &lt;canvas id="stage"&gt; — three.js target
  &lt;canvas id="fx-raster"&gt;, &lt;canvas id="fx-trace"&gt;, &lt;canvas id="fx-rate"&gt; — 2D overlay canvases, only visible/laid out in Neuron mode
  &lt;aside id="side-panel"&gt; — mode-specific content, swapped by the mode controller: Pathway list+transport, Atlas region list+search+lesion toggle, Neuron presets+sliders
  &lt;section id="explain-panel"&gt; — persistent "Explain this" surface, always present, its innerHTML replaced by whichever controller is active; content is produced via a shared linkTerms(html) helper so every rendered explanation gets glossary spans automatically
  &lt;dialog id="glossary-popover"&gt; (or a positioned div) — opens near a clicked .term span
  &lt;aside id="how-drawer"&gt; — slide-in panel: Rendering, Timing model, Neuron equations, Metaphor-vs-physiology / misconceptions (from accuracy_pitfalls), full A-Z glossary browser (safety net for coverage)
  &lt;div id="webgl-lost-banner" hidden&gt; — shown on 'webglcontextlost'
  &lt;script type="module"&gt;
